# NPN classes of the 4-input Boolean functions and their minimum networks
# of 3-input tables (npn.c).  The tool reports 222 classes and that every
# class's representative network was proved minimum.  A bitwise cone of
# four leaves is rewritten as its class's network of LUT3 tables; the
# rewrite gets a second opinion from SAT in find, and a model with no
# table instruction must leave the cone alone.
gates npn
m(a: u32, b: u32, c: u32, d: u32) = (a & b) | (a & c) | (a & d) | (b & c) | (b & d) | (c & d)
find m 1
model nolut : gt1030 { nofuse lop3 }
use nolut
find m 1
use gt1030
